there is a story that's hugely important  but not necessarily for the reasons a  lot of people think the Chinese doctor  who was the whistleblower about  coronavirus has died now immediately a  ton of articles and a ton of people  started saying or implying the Chinese  government killed the doctor and that  that's the scandal the doctor appears to  have genuinely died of coronavirus  himself which he contracted while  working at Wuhan central hospital in  China the scandal and the controversy is  that the Chinese government appears to  have sent police to tell him to shut up  about corona virus after he sent out a  warning via chat group to other doctors  on December 30th about coronavirus we're  talking about 34 year old doctor Lee wen  Yan Liang who was an ophthalmologist  noticed seven cases of a virus that  looked to him like SARS he sent the  message to doctors in a chat group  saying you should wear protective  clothing when you're with patients  four days later as reported by the BBC  he was summoned by the Public Security  Bureau where he was told to sign a  letter which accused him of quote making  false comments that had quote severely  disturbed the social order he was one of  eight people who police say were being  investigated for spreading rumors  local authorities later apologized to  him because of course he was completely  right about coronavirus but more  importantly a few days later on January  10th he started coughing then he had a  fever then he was in the hospital  diagnosed with corona virus on the 30th  of January and ultimately has passed  away so as of right now I do not believe  that the Chinese government killed him I  believe he died of exactly what he was  worried about which is coronavirus  contracted from patients the real  concern is that the Chinese government  has prioritized silencing doctors rather  than immediately moving to deal with  coronavirus and I want to be really  careful because the entire coronavirus  story has been used in some enclaves to  justify discriminatory and disguise  ding comments about Chinese people and  Chinese culture that's not what I'm  doing this is a critique of the Chinese  government  now just to circle back around to the  conspiracy theory piece that the Chinese  government killed this guy to silence  him that he didn't die of coronaviruses  of co of coronavirus i'm not blind to  the atrocities committed by the chinese  government over the last many decades  I'm not pretending they don't exist we  don't have evidence that that's what  happened so I don't believe that it is  prudent or responsible to push it now  there are some people who said you know  this guy was 34 coronavirus is really  killing little kids and the elderly how  did a 34 year old die of it that's  mostly true but there are people of just  sort of medium ages that have died of  coronavirus I'm not ignoring the  possibility that there is more to this  but right now it does not seem  responsible to push that the Chinese  government killed this guy it does seem  that the Chinese government was more  concerned with covering up the existence  of coronavirus early on then in moving  quickly and swiftly to actually deal  with it the latest numbers 38,000 cases  815 deaths nearly 3,000 people have  recovered so far so far there is a lower  death rate with coronavirus than with  SARS the death rate is about two percent  with SARS it was about 10 to 15 percent  but the number of infections is  significantly larger and more than  likely it's going to end up killing many  more people very very sad what's going  on and certainly any time a government  works to cover something up rather than  to actually deal with it it is  concerning for the entire world as we  are quickly seeing cases start to spread  all over the world
 

